.mcp.json
# ...and every variant of it. A .mcp.json.hidden appeared in the working tree on 10 Aug 2026
# while an agent was running `git add -A`; the exact name `.mcp.json` did not match it, so a
# file holding the live read-only Postgres URI was one wildcard away from GitHub. A credential
# committed is exposed RETROACTIVELY - git keeps the history, and only rotation undoes it.
.mcp.json*
bridge/token.txt*
bridge/bridge.err.log
bridge/bridge.log
bridge/token.txt
dist/
env/
node_modules/
workbook_extract/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Netlify CLI state — build artefact, never source (added 8 Aug 2026)
app/web/.netlify/
# Python bytecode from tools/
**/__pycache__/
# Downloaded PDF cache for the document parsers — regenerable from storage
tools/documents/.cache/
